# DOGGYWOOD HERO FREEZE

The current rendered desktop hero is final and is the source of truth.

It overrides every earlier hero proportion instruction, including two-thirds / one-third.

Do not redesign, rebalance, resize, or reinterpret it.

Do not apply earlier hero specifications that conflict with the current implementation.

## Frozen zone

Everything from the top of the header through the bottom of the trust strip is frozen.

Future Phase 2 work begins below the trust strip.

Protected unless the prompt specifically names the hero and explicitly instructs a change:

- `.dw-hero`
- `.dw-hero-desktop`
- `.dw-hero-photo-viewport`
- `.dw-hero-photo-card`
- `.dw-hero-photo`
- `.dw-hero-inner`
- `.dw-hero-copy`
- `LaunchHeader`
- the trust strip immediately below the hero (`$500 EVERY MONTH` / `SHOW OFF YOUR PUP` / `MOST UPVOTES WINS`)

If a global style change would affect the hero, scope the new styles so the approved hero remains visually identical.

## Do not change

Header: logo asset `/brand/doggywood-logo.webp`, logo size, nav placement/labels, both right buttons, spacing, height, typography, button dimensions. No arrows.

Hero grid: keep the current 46% / 54% columns. Do not change to two-thirds / one-third or any other ratio.

Hero height: keep `520px`. No `min-height` viewport sizing. Do not make it taller or shorter.

Left column: badge `WIN $500 THIS MONTH!`; headline lines `Your Dog’s Shot` / `at Fame Starts` / `Here.`; current font, size, weight, line-height, black treatment, yellow `Starts` and `Here.`; current body copy; CTA `ENTER THIS MONTH'S CONTEST` at current width, height, color, and placement. No arrow.

Right image: `/brand/doggywood-mobile-hero.webp` in the rounded feature card. Keep current crop, dog size/position, tag, hills, palms, sky, sign, radius, frame, `object-fit`, and `object-position: 50% 46%`. Do not replace, regenerate, or rebuild from separate assets. No fade, mask, overlay, blur, opacity, or gradient.

Spacing: do not alter gaps between badge/headline, headline/body, body/CTA, left column/right image, or hero/trust strip.

Trust strip: keep the three items, icons, icon size, typography, dividers, cream background, height, and spacing. No fourth item.

Mobile hero remains independently locked.

Exact supplied Doggywood and Verify.Dog logo assets are mandatory. Never recreate, approximate, generate, or replace them with styled text.

## Desktop check

Verify at 1920, 1600, 1440, and 1024. Do not modify the hero just because text wraps differently at narrower desktop widths unless there is an actual overflow defect.

Before declaring any later phase complete, confirm header, logo, hero copy, hero dimensions, image, image crop, CTA, and trust strip are unchanged. If any of those changed, restore them first.
